      <Comment source="AU4FS-4, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: CPD-15225 &quot;Cyclic di-3&apos;,5&apos;-adenylate&quot;| (c-di-AMP) is a signaling molecule predominantly produced by Gram-positive bacteria belonging to the Firmicutes and Actinobacteria, although there have been several reports about its biosynthesis by some Gram-negative bacteria. It is involved in regulating a number of physiological processes including osmotic pressure, stress response, and potassium transport |CITS: [18439896][18714086][20508090][20508090][23812326][22529992][23631912][24566626]|. It is synthesized from two molecules of ATP by |FRAME: EC-2.7.7.85|, and is hydrolyzed by |FRAME: EC-3.1.4.59| into |FRAME: CPD-21427| (pApA) |CITS: [18439896][19901023][20508090][21909268][25869574][26773214]|.</Comment>
